%S A399866 1,2,3,4,6,7,9,11,12,14,15,16,18,20,21,22,24,25,27,29,30,31,33,34,36,
%T A399866 38,39,41,42,43,45,47,48,50,51,52,54,56,57,59,60,61,63,65,66,68,69,70,
%U A399866 72,74,75,76,78,79,81,83,84,85,87,88,90,92,93,94,96,97,99,101,102,103
%N A399866 a(1) = 1; a(n+1) is the smallest integer greater than a(n) such that: a(k) + a(k+3) is not a term for any k.
%H A399866 Hoang Xuan Thanh, <a href="/A399866/a399866_2.pdf">Exact Closed-Form Characterization and Binary Fractal Dynamics of the Greedy Sequence Avoiding a(k) + a(k + 3)</a>.
%F A399866 a(n) = floor((3*n-1)/2) - (n mod 2) - [(n mod 6)=0] - [(n mod 6)=4]*[(floor(log_2(floor((n-1)/3))) mod 2) = 0], for n >= 4.
%o A399866 (PARI) a(n) = (3*n-1)\2 - ((n%2) + (n%6==0) + (n%6==4)*(#binary((n-1)\3)%2)) + (n==1)
%Y A399866 Cf. Sequences avoiding a forbidden sum for any pair at distance k: A001651 (k=1) (upper bound), A399801 (k=2), this sequence (k=3), A399049 (k=4).
%Y A399866 Cf. Sequences avoiding a forbidden sum for any m consecutive terms: A001651 (m=2), A394576 (m=3), A394676 (m=4).
%K A399866 nonn,easy,new
%O A399866 1,2
